From: arch-m4 project
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tipd: use the common device for connector lookup

Wallace's SPMI transport moves probe into tps6598x_probe_common(dev, ...),
but retains an I2C-only connector lookup. i2c_verify_client(dev) returns
NULL for an SPMI device, so deriving &client->dev is invalid on that path.
Use the bus-neutral device argument, as the rest of the common probe does.
The guarded I2C adapter capability check remains unchanged.

Local correction against Linux e9d2237cd064e6d086d938cd9c85e0c963cf7291 plus:
https://github.com/damsleth/wallace/blob/55f116dd0e0f28d1412c6be728a101f7d861c473/patches/0001-usb-typec-tps6598x-add-SPMI-transport-for-T6040-SN20.patch

This fixes a source-level invalid-pointer bug. Native SPMI controller bring-up
and USB device enumeration still require hardware validation.

--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tipd/core.c
@@ -1820,7 +1820,7 @@
 	 * with existing DT files, we work around this by deleting any
 	 * fwnode_links to/from this fwnode.
 	 */
-	fwnode = device_get_named_child_node(&client->dev, "connector");
+	fwnode = device_get_named_child_node(dev, "connector");
 	if (fwnode)
 		fw_devlink_purge_absent_suppliers(fwnode);
 
